  "ARGUMENT": "a molecule offers Binomial(4, q) hops per step, so p_hop on average, and lives (1-mu)/mu steps; a fraction eps of offered hops is refused, and by exchangeability within a cell each offered hop is refused with probability eps on average. E[R] = p_hop * eps * (1-mu)/mu, and Markov gives P(R >= 1) <= E[R]. No distributional assumption is used.",
